  "premise_review": [
    "The actual stored-index existence theorem preserves all exact fully qualified implicit C : SiteCategory, J : GrothendieckTopology C, F : SheafOfSpectra J, D : SheafSpectrumOperator F and W : WittComplex parameters, and explicit B : ArithmeticBoundaryIndexBridge D W.",
    "The conclusion is exactly ∃ I : WittValuedCrystallineIndex D W, I = B.index, with its unchanged qualified imported proof term. The fully read underlying theorem supplies the already stored witness B.index and rfl; no index is computed from arithmetic data.",
    "The other wrapper is a genuine conditional proof of B.arithmeticDataSupportsIndex, forwarding the original witness-projection theorem. That support field is an arbitrary proposition, with no formula about arithmeticSource, optional arithmetic contracts or index. It remains exact archive-only.",
    "Unlike the same-file review142 record source, this wrapper already imports Folder.CrystallineIndex.ArithmeticBoundaryBridge, which supplies its complete legacy B type. Materializing the concrete existence theorem requires no new self-provider import, weakened type or replacement provider.",
    "Full captured record/source142 and both original direct providers were read: optional arithmetic contracts need not be present or related to index; genuine BSD equalities and stored Witt-element/index existence proofs are acknowledged without constructing arithmetic or cohomological semantics.",
    "Both source proof terms, all hypotheses and qualified historical names are preserved exactly. The new review142 archive record is not installed as a provider, and no new GRWTSK replacement for the imported types or theorem is substituted.",
    "No actual arithmetic-to-Witt construction, arithmetic certificate, index computation, cohomology/K-theory interpretation, human review, compilation or mathematical acceptance is asserted. Exact historical dependency resolution remains unreplayed."
  ],
